<title>USA: North Central Texas Health $52 mln repriced.</title>
<headline>North Central Texas Health $52 mln repriced.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>First Southwest Co said it repriced a $52 million North Central Texas Health Facilities Development Corporation hospital revenue bond issue, Series 1997, for Zale Lipshy University Hospital project, cutting the top yield in 2019 to 5.85 percent from 5.90 percent.</p>
<p>NORTH CENTRAL TEXAS HEALTH</p>
<p>RE: $52,210,000*</p>
<p>FACILITIES DEVELOPMENT CORPORATION</p>
